According to the documented rule for conformance.kernel.recovery, 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text'. In the input, the object {"a": 1} is inside the code fence, so it is the scored object. In the rewritten text, the code fence is empty, so no object is inside, and there is no top-level object, resulting in NO_OBJECT. Thus the recovered object moves from {"a": 1} to NO_OBJECT.